# The Next.js web app (this project's Vercel deployment) never reads from
# mobile/ — it's a separate Expo/React Native app in the same repo. Its own
# mobile/.gitignore excludes node_modules/ and the native android/ios build
# output from git, but the Vercel CLI's upload step doesn't honor nested
# .gitignore files, only the root one plus this file — so a local Android
# build under mobile/android/app/build (gradle intermediates, some 200MB+
# per .so file) was getting swept into the upload and failing with "File
# size limit exceeded (100 MB)". Excluding the whole directory here since
# none of it belongs in a Next.js deployment anyway.
/mobile
